#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179494 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "02ae40ba-a02c-5025-9597-1968322f2421" :question/math-academy-id "e-2279" :question/problem "In a ballet school, the ratio of the number of students with black hair to the total number of students is $5: 8.$ If there are $25$ students with black hair, how many students are there in ballet school who don't have black hair?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}8}$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}}{{\\color{red}8}}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of students with black hair and the denominator represents the total number of students.\n\nWe know that there are $25$ students with black hair, so we want to make a numerator of $25.$ We can do this by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}\\times 5}{{\\color{red}8}\\times 5} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}25}}{{\\color{red}40}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since there are $25$ students with black hair, there must be $40$ students at the ballet school. Of this amount, the number of students who do not have black hair is\n\n$$\n40 - 25 = 15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179495 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "4aeb615e-16a1-5170-be5e-fe0f63a5d895" :question/math-academy-id "e-2280" :question/problem "Noah has $42$ toy blocks, of which $\\dfrac{5}{7}$ are blue, and the rest are green. How many green blocks does Noah have?" :question/worked-solution "Explanation:\n\nWe are given that the ratio of blue blocks to the total number of blocks is $\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}}{{\\color{red}7}}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of blue blocks, and the denominator represents   the total number of blocks .\n\nWe can make a denominator of $42$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $6{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}\\times 6}{{\\color{red}7}\\times 6} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}30}}{{\\color{red}42}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $30$ blue blocks. \n\nSo the number of green blocks is\n\n$$\n42 - 30 = 12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a71d876-052d-58a1-b34d-f38c05859375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272482} {:answer/id #uuid "1262f3a1-1ef9-5e94-acf7-e2e3dabf8d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272552} {:answer/id #uuid "3a1181eb-e541-5a91-b732-f8477165807d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272891} {:answer/id #uuid "4c474222-0096-5a01-bdfc-a46a7d6adee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273028} {:answer/id #uuid "97cd86eb-fc0b-59f4-bd1d-84c292397d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a1181eb-e541-5a91-b732-f8477165807d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272891} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7177293-97a8-5f50-a884-9c2e6ddbf2a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d66fb6cc-b6c6-55ab-abc9-f32c6026bbc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-147213" :question/problem "A bag contains blue and green buttons. The ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $2:7.$ If there are $14$ blue buttons,  how many green buttons are in the bag?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $\\frac{2}{7}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of blue buttons, and the denominator represents the total number of buttons.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $14$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 7}{7\\times 7}=\\frac{14}{49}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $49$ buttons in the bag. \nSo, the number of green buttons is\n\n$$\n49-14=35.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8bcb70-f387-57f1-b985-1c057ae42b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178955} {:answer/id #uuid "f9460abe-6362-5427-80a3-210edfa18733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178956} {:answer/id #uuid "11685da2-bde8-5f24-bd85-d223b82aec5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178957} {:answer/id #uuid "1b9f3e90-4c5d-534d-b403-a3f64b2c8e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178958} {:answer/id #uuid "32edb789-dd22-5410-b835-5d4df4b73c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178959}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e2ad40bb-4d57-528e-ad01-c6b43912c1bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178954}] :question/id #uuid "6419cc5c-f55d-5667-812d-e81bfe685d0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-60194" :question/problem "In Noheli's red and white rose garden, $\\frac{3}{10}$ of the roses are red. If there are a total of $90$ roses in the garden, how many white roses are there?"}]}
